* TUBE COMP - DATASHEET-ANCHORED VALVE CELLS (rev B / 2026-11-12)
* These models correct the original hard 6BC8 cutoff and 6CG7 gain error.
* A per-device parametric fit is NOT proof of a factory-original Altec unit.
* 6BC8 model from published Sylvania plate-curve Koren parameter candidate,
* also stored in models/6bc8_sylvania_curve_candidate.lib (source there).
* See RCA 6BC8 datasheet: https://frank.pocnet.net/sheets/049/6/6BC8.pdf
* The model at Va=150V has nonzero conduction at Vg=-10V; this is essential
* for remote-cutoff gain reduction across many tens of dB.
.subckt V6BC8 P G K
BPL P K I={20.19891536u*pow(uramp(V(P,K)*ln(1+exp(1.794225622*(1+54.16463004*V(G,K)/sqrt(922.2704089+V(P,K)*V(P,K)))))/1.794225622),1.439822572)}
Rleak P K 1000Meg
CGK G K 3.9p
CGA G P 3.7p
CPK P K 1.8p
.ends V6BC8

* 6BC8 semiremote-cutoff candidate, fitted at TWO operating conditions.
* This optional variant adds a very weak low-gm plate-current branch,
* representing the low-mu sections of the semiremote-cutoff grid.
* Numerical fit anchors:
*  - RCA sheet at Va=150V and Rk=220R: Ip approx 10mA and gm=6200umho,
*    grid grounded -> Vgk approx -2.2V; rp approx 5.3k.
*  - factory 436C drawing at idle: 65V plates, (210-65)/47k=3.085mA,
*    grid-cathode about -1V with 34R shared cathode.
*  - RCA -13V sensitivity: gm about 50umho.
*  - factory 20dB compressed: 285V plates, 290V plate-feed, 47k loads
*    => (290-285)/47k = 0.1064mA PER HALF at about -30V bias.
* Single-Koren V6BC8 yields only 0.000172mA at this last anchor (x618 low).
* Fitted monotonic remote tail is NOT a manufacturer's plate curve;
* independently verify against a real 6BC8 at the deep-negative bias.
* DC positive grid current, heaters, and alternate supply sag are unmodeled.
.subckt V6BC8_REMOTE P G K
BPL P K I={20.2365654u*pow(uramp(V(P,K)*ln(1+exp(1.794225622*(1+59.22382604*V(G,K)/sqrt(922.2704089+V(P,K)*V(P,K)))))/1.794225622),1.439822572)+0.96348024m*pow(uramp(V(P,K)/150),1.69329672)/(1+exp(-(V(G,K)+14.76054299)/4.6849283))}
Rleak P K 1000Meg
CGK G K 3.9p
CGA G P 3.7p
CPK P K 1.8p
.ends V6BC8_REMOTE

* 6CG7: CC0 model fitted by Circuit Codex to published RCA anchor:
* Va=250V / Vg=-8V -> 9mA, 2600umho, mu=20.
* Further checkpoints at 90V/0V and 250V/-12.5V are approximate.
* Upstream model: https://github.com/TheAnalogMaker/circuit-codex/blob/main/models/6cg7.inc
* License: CC0 1.0 Universal. Heater and positive grid current not modeled.
.subckt V6CG7 P G K
BPL P K I={pow(uramp((V(P,K)/127.155)*ln(1+exp(127.155*(1/20+V(G,K)/sqrt(300+V(P,K)*V(P,K)))))),1.5)/1134.77}
Rleak P K 1000Meg
CGK G K 2.3p
CGA G P 4p
CPK P K 2.2p
.ends V6CG7

* Alternative independently published 6CG7 plate-curve candidate: GE 1963.
* The GE Koren parameters (MU=21.86 EX=1.319 KG1=1248.5 KP=140.12
* KVB=300) originate in GE-derived triode libraries. They are a
* cross-check candidate, NOT a proof of the particular Altec factory tube.
* Do not silently replace the RCA candidate until multiple anchor points
* and the circuit operating-point measurements have been compared.
.subckt V6CG7_GE P G K
BPL P K I={pow(uramp((V(P,K)/140.12)*ln(1+exp(140.12*(1/21.86+V(G,K)/sqrt(300+V(P,K)*V(P,K)))))),1.319)/1248.5}
Rleak P K 1000Meg
CGK G K 2.9p
CGA G P 4.7p
CPK P K 2.7p
.ends V6CG7_GE

* 6AL5 diode remains a provisional forward characteristic.
* Diode's 3.2-3.6pF element capacitance comes from Sylvania 6AL5 sheet.
* Equivalent Is/N/Rs NOT a calibrated plate-current curve.
.model D6AL5 D(Is=3n N=1.55 Rs=600 Cjo=3.4p M=0.40 Tt=65n)
